= Software — Simple =

'''Software''' is the non-physical part of a computing system that tells computers what to do.

Software includes [[Program (computing)/Simple|programs]]. A larger software system can also include libraries, configuration, data definitions, tests, and other files needed to build or operate it.

Hardware is the physical equipment, such as processors, memory chips, disks, sensors, or screens. Software uses hardware to produce behavior.

Examples of software include:

* operating systems;
* web browsers;
* games;
* phone apps;
* databases;
* cloud services;
* software inside vehicles and appliances.

Software changes over time. Developers use [[Version control/Simple|version control]] to record revisions, compare changes, and work together.

The exact boundary of "software" depends on what system is being discussed. For some purposes documentation or deployment configuration is part of the software; for others it is treated separately.

